      "content": "If you can't change the walls or the silence, perhaps you can change what you do *inside* them. Waiting for an exit that isn't coming is exhausting; it's a passive form of suffering. Instead of waiting for the movie to end, what if you decided to write the next scene? A small, deliberate action—a change in your routine, a different kind of focus—can sometimes be the only way to break the inertia of the loop.",
      "source": "target",
